    "body": "## 📝 Provide a description of the new feature\r\n\r\n_What is the expected behavior of the proposed feature?  What is the scenario this would be used?_\r\n\r\nI find myself frequently juggling with URLs which get pasted to the clipboard and then inserted into some browser-window, so (just as a proof-of-concept) I wrote a little tool (independ of PT) which observes the clipboard and if it finds one, suggests to open - which I can then accept of neglect. I was unsure whether this would be practical of if I would get bombarded with prompts that I don't use. But after a few wks of using this, I still like the idea and would like to take it further - and that is beyond my level of knowledge, beyond the capabilities of the environment I worked on etc., and it also feels like PT Run would be a more obvious home for such functionality. Which is why I opened this issue.\r\n\r\nI suggest that PT Run should observe the clipboard and if it finds a new entry commencing with `http[s]:`, it should display a dialog that offers a choice of browsers (either as \"found on the system\" or configured by the user) which could open this URL. The dialog also has a Cancel-Button. Ideally there should be a configurable timeout after which the dialog will close.\r\n\r\nAs a milder form (if the observer is disabled through a config-option), it would be good if when entering such URLs into PTs Search-Field there was a choice of browser to open the URL with.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to see this feature implemented, add a 👍 reaction to this post.\r\n",
